<!--
  sui-button — SUI port of ship-button. Tone-driven control button with five
  visual variants (default / solid / soft / outline / ghost), four sizes
  (xs / sm / md / lg), and loading / disabled / pressed / expanded ARIA
  states. Mirrors the native button surface (type / submit / reset).

  Visible styling covered by the new collapsed SFC shape (sx + variants +
  framework tone + size contracts):
    - tone (free framework contract) drives bg / fg / border / contrast.
    - size (free framework contract) drives min-h, padding, font-size.
    - Variant block overrides the host baseline per variant:
        default  - bg:background, fg:foreground, border, shadow-xs
        solid    - bg:tone, fg:tone-contrast, border:tone, shadow-xs
        soft     - bg:tone-bg, fg:tone-fg, border:tone-border
        outline  - fg:tone-fg, border:tone (bg falls through to baseline)
        ghost    - no override (uses host baseline: bg:tone-bg, border:none)
    - Element sx carries the always-on baseline:
        display:inline-flex, radius:md, cursor:pointer, position:relative,
        min-h:size-h, px:size-px, text:size-fs, weight:medium, py:0.
    - Hover / focus / disabled are state prefixes on the same sx:
        hover:bg:hover-bg
        focus:ring:primary
        disabled:cursor:not-allowed, disabled:bg:muted, disabled:fg:muted-foreground
    - motion:hover with scale spring:snappy AOT-bakes the hover scale.

  Open irreducibles (see MIGRATION-NOTES.md at the repo root) - these visuals
  are OMITTED in this migration because the language today cannot express
  them; the orchestrator closes each gap:
    1. [part='button'] baseline properties - background:transparent,
       border:1px solid transparent, isolation:isolate, font-family,
       line-height:1, letter-spacing, user-select, white-space. No part
       allowed; sx has no transparent, font-family, line-height,
       letter-spacing, user-select, white-space.
    2. Multi-property transition on bg / border / shadow / transform. sx
       has no transition shorthand; the runtime already covers a single
       reduced-motion fallback but not the four properties in concert.
    3. Hover transform translateY(-1px) and active transform
       translateY(1px) scale(0.98). sx has no transform utility; the
       motion hover scale covers scale only.
    4. Disabled filter saturate(0.6). sx has no filter; the color side
       moves into the disabled state prefix.
    5. Per-variant hover background colors. The variants body sx lowers
       through lower_variant_sx (prop:tok pairs only, no state prefix),
       so a per-variant hover rule cannot be authored. Hover falls back
       to a single host-level hover:bg:hover-bg.
    6. Variant-specific disabled override for ghost and outline
       (background:transparent). The variants selector grammar lacks
       pseudo-class selectors; disabled:bg:muted applies globally.
    7. Loading state - :host(loading) cursor:progress and content
       opacity:0. loading is not a state prefix; the cursor moves to the
       disabled-style not-allowed cursor (covers it functionally).
    8. Icon-only shape - :host(data-icon-only) padding-inline:0,
       width:var(--btn-h), min-width:var(--btn-h). sx has no width / height
       with theme channels; the icon-only override would need a per-size
       selector the variant grammar lacks.
    9. Spinner (keyframe animation + absolute positioning + opacity:0 of
       content while loading). @keyframes is irreducible per the brief;
       the loading conditional block is dropped entirely.
   10. .content inner-row gap per size (xs:space-1, sm:space-1_5,
       md:space-2, lg:space-2). The row gap attribute is a fixed token
       (0 to 8, integer-only) and cannot read the framework size-gap
       channel; the row uses gap=2 as a static default.
   11. ::slotted([slot='trailing']) layout - display:inline-flex,
       align-items:center, flex:0 0 auto. sx has no ::slotted; the slot
       author is responsible for their icon's own sizing.
   12. vertical-align:middle on the host. align is intentionally absent
       from sx (layout = primitives); the host baseline loses
       vertical-align.
   13. Per-size font-weight channel (btn-fw). The framework size channels
       are size-h / size-px / size-fs / size-gap only; btn-fw was a local
       theme channel. The current values were font-weight-medium across
       every size, so weight:medium is functionally equivalent.

  Controller: NONE. The button is stateless beyond the ARIA attrs it
  mirrors; no event dispatch was previously wired and none is added
  here. Consumers attach their own listeners via the onclick attribute.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    tone,
    size,
    variant: 'default' | 'solid' | 'soft' | 'outline' | 'ghost',
    type: 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset',
    disabled: bool,
    loading: bool,
    label: string,
    pressed: 'false' | 'true' | 'mixed',
    expanded: string,
  },
  variants: {
    variant: {
      default: 'bg:background border:border fg:foreground shadow:xs',
      solid:   'bg:tone      border:tone   fg:tone-contrast shadow:xs',
      soft:    'bg:tone-bg   border:tone-border fg:tone-fg',
      outline: 'border:tone  fg:tone-fg',
    },
  }
}</component>

<button
  type={type()}
  disabled={disabled() || loading()}
  motion:hover={{ scale: 'spring:snappy' }}
  aria-busy={loading() ? 'true' : 'false'}
  aria-disabled={(disabled() || loading()) ? 'true' : 'false'}
  aria-label={label()}
  aria-pressed={pressed()}
  aria-expanded={expanded()}
  sx="
    display:inline-flex
    radius:md
    cursor:pointer
    position:relative
    min-h:size-h
    px:size-px
    text:size-fs
    weight:medium
    py:0
    bg:tone-bg
    border:none
    fg:tone-fg
    hover:bg:hover-bg
    focus:ring:primary
    disabled:cursor:not-allowed
    disabled:bg:muted
    disabled:fg:muted-foreground
  "
>
  <row align="center" justify="center" gap="2">
    <slot name="leading"></slot>
    <slot reflect-empty="data-icon-only"></slot>
    <slot name="trailing"></slot>
  </row>
</button>